# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git normalizes text files to LF in the object database and checks them out
# with LF in the working tree, overriding any user-level core.autocrlf
# setting. This keeps the repository byte-identical on Windows, macOS, and
# Linux, and it is required by tooling that is configured for LF: Ruff's
# formatter runs with line-ending = "lf", so a CRLF working tree fails
# `ruff format --check` even when the committed blobs are already correct.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be normalized: doing so corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.parquet binary
*.pkl binary
*.joblib binary
*.pt binary
*.pth binary
*.onnx binary
*.mlmodel binary
